Upstream files NOT in this repository
-------------------------------------
  - Arcade-Galaxian.sv (MiSTer's top level): the Tango wrapper replaces it.
  - The game logic -- rtl/galaxian.vhd, mc_adec.vhd, mc_bram.vhd, mc_col_pal.vhd, mc_hv_count.vhd, mc_inport.vhd,
    mc_ld_pls.vhd, mc_logic.vhd, mc_missile.vhd, mc_sound_a.vhd, mc_sound_b.vhd, mc_stars.vhd, mc_video.vhd,
    kb_synth.vhd, mc_sound_vco.vhd, sine_package.vhd -- and the sample tables ROM/FIR.vhd and ROM/HIT.vhd: none of
    them is in this repository, in whole or in part.  The core's game logic is the Tango authors' own RTL.
  - rtl/pause.v, rtl/dpram.vhd, rtl/spram.vhd, rtl/mc_clocks.vhd, rtl/ttl_*.vhd, rtl/pll*, the T80 files the core
    does not instantiate (T80s, T80a, T80as, T80pa, T80sed, T8080se, GBse, Z80, T16450), sys/: not used.


Other material
--------------
  - rtl/tango/tg16_aboost.v: the Audio Boost stage, copied from tg16-tango by way of scramble-tango (the same
    authors), GPL-3.0-or-later as its header says: a port of the knee compressor of MiSTer's TurboGrafx16_MiSTer
    (TurboGrafx16.sv compr(), copyright (C) 2017-2019 Sorgelig).
  - tools/gen_gx_dbg_ov.py and the file it writes, rtl/tango/gx_dbg_ov.v (the dev build's debug overlay; release
    builds do not include it): adapted from tg16-tango tools/gen_tg16_dbg_ov.py (the same authors); its 5 x 7 glyphs
    were drawn for that file.
  - rtl/tango_galaxian.v, build/build_galaxian.sh, build/galaxian_ddr3.sdc: the Tango wrapper, its build and its
    timing constraints, adapted from scramble-tango (rtl/tango_scramble.v, build/build_scramble.sh,
    build/scramble_ddr3.sdc) and galaga-tango (rtl/tango_galaga.v, hiscore.v's wiring), the same authors.
  - build/build_galaxian.sh also takes from the Arcade Template skeleton the port started from, arcade-template-tango
    (GPL-2.0-or-later, the Tango authors), here under GPL-3.0-or-later as that licence's "any later version"
    allows.


ROM data: the games' ROMs and PROMs are not in this repository or in a bitstream built from it; a user supplies them
as MAME zips, assembled at run time by the Tango firmware from the .mra.  The one exception is the two homebrew .mra
files, mra/Clean Sweep.mra and mra/Mr. Do Nightmare.mra: they carry their game program as inline hex in rom index 0,
as published in MiSTer's Arcade-Galaxian release (MiSTer-devel/Arcade-Galaxian_MiSTer, releases/); their <rom>
entries are MiSTer's, unchanged (the Tango .mra changes only the switches' default, the buttons and the header
comment).  No licence statement for that program data is given upstream, and none is
claimed here.  There is no other ROM data in this repository.
